{title: Not Ashamed of My Chains}
{subtitle: 2 Timothy 1:18; 1:17; 1:16; 4:19; 1:15–18}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] |
| [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Everyone in Asia turned a[Bb/D]way
[Cm7]Phygelus and Hermogenes [Cm7/Bb]did [Ab]flee
[Eb]But he searched hard until he [Bb/D]found me
In the [Ab]prison where I [Bb]was to [Eb]be
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
May the [Ab]Lord show mer[Bb]cy to his [Eb]house
For he [Ab]often refreshed [Bb]me somehow
He was [Cm7]not [Ab]ashamed of my chains
[Bb]Faithful in the [Cm7]wind and in the [Bb]rains
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You [Ab]know well his service in [Bb]Ephesus
A de[Eb]vo[Eb]tion that no one can refuse
He came [Bb/D]to Rome to seek [Cm7]me out
And brought com[Cm7/Bb]fort and qui[Ab]et [Eb]about
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
May the Lord show mer[Bb/D]cy to his [Ab]house
For he [Bb]often re[Eb]freshed me some[Ab]how
He was [Bb]not ashamed [Eb]of my chains
[Ab]Faithful in the [Bb]wind and in [Cm7]the [Ab]rains
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
May the Lord [Bb]grant him mer[Cm7]cy on that [Bb]Day
For [Ab]the faithfulness he [Bb]chose to [Eb]pay [Cm7][Bb][Ab][Bb][Cm7][Bb][Ab]
Greet Prisca and [Bb]Aquila [Eb]too
And [Ab]the household [Bb]standing firm and [Cm7]true
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]May the [Bb]Lord show mercy [Cm7]to his [Bb]house
For [Ab]he often re[Bb]freshed me some[Eb]how
He [Ab]was not as[Bb]hamed of my [Eb]chains
Faith[Ab]ful in the wind [Bb]and in the [Cm7]rains
{end_of_chorus}

